hadiths[129]{hadithnumber,text}:
"790","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: Jibril came to me and said: O Muhammad! Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has cursed wine, its presser, the one who has it pressed, its drinker, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, its buyer, its cupbearer, and the one who asks for it to be served."
"791","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Avoid wine, for it is the key to all evil."
"792","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah, she said: They used to, in the Days of Ignorance, when they performed the 'Aqiqah for a child, dye a piece of cotton with the blood of the 'Aqiqah, and when they shaved the child's head they would place it on his head. So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Put perfume in place of the blood, meaning: on the child's head on the day of slaughtering for him."
"793","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ibn 'Umar, raised to the Prophet: Two dead things and two bloods have been made lawful to us. As for the two dead things, they are the fish and the locust, and as for the two bloods, they are the liver and the spleen."
"794","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: Delay the pregnant camels, for the hand is tied and the leg is bound."
"795","[AI-translation] From 'Umar ibn Abi Salamah that he entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, while he had food. He said: Draw near, O my son, mention the name of Allah, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is in front of you."
"796","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: When the servant of one of you prepares his food and he bears its heat and cold, let him make him sit with him. If he refuses, let him hand him a morsel in his hand."
"797","[AI-translation] From Ibn Jurayj who said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, saying: I heard Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: When one of you eats food, let him not wipe his hand until he licks it or has it licked. And no bowl should be lifted until it is licked or has it licked, for the last of the food contains blessing."
"798","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: When the servant of one of you comes with his food, let him make him sit with him; if he does not make him sit with him, let him hand him some of it."
"799","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: When the servant of one of you comes with his food, let him make him sit with him and let him hand him a morsel or two, for he handled its preparation and its heat."
"800","[AI-translation] Narrated from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, stopped at him: When the servant of one of you comes with his food, let him seat him with him or let him hand him some of it, for he is the one who handled its heat and its smoke."
"801","[AI-translation] From Ibn Jurayj who said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, he heard Jabir say: I heard the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, say: When one of you invites his brother to food, let him accept; if he wishes, he may eat, and if he wishes, he may leave it."
"802","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: When one of you is invited to food, let him accept. If he is not fasting, let him eat, and if he is fasting, let him pray."
"803","[AI-translation] Khushani that the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: When you shoot game and retrieve it after three nights, and your arrow is in it, eat it, as long as it has not become rotten."
"804","[AI-translation] Narrated Samrah bin Jundub that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: If you give your family an evening drink of milk, then avoid what Allah has prohibited of carrion."
"805","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: When you travel through fertile land, give the mounts their right, and when you travel through barren land, hasten on them. And travel by night, for the land is folded up at night. And when you halt to rest, do not halt on the main road, for it is the refuge of every creature."
"806","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When one of you drinks, let him not breathe into the vessel. And if he wishes to drink again, let him move the vessel away, then let him return to it if he wishes."
"807","[AI-translation] Narrated Umm Salamah that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When you drink milk, rinse your mouth, for it has fat."
"808","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: When one of you offers a sacrifice, let him eat from his sacrificial animal."
"809","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When you cook meat, increase the broth or the water, for it is more abundant and reaches further for the neighbors."
"810","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah that he heard the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) say: When one of you eats and his morsel falls from his hand, let him wipe off whatever is harmful on it and eat it, and not leave it for the devil. And he should not wipe his hand with a cloth until he licks his hand, for a man does not know in which part of his food the blessing lies. And the devil lies in wait for people—or for man—in all things, even at his meal or his food. And he should not lift the bowl until he licks it or has it licked, for there is blessing in the latter part of the food."
"811","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: When a fly falls into the drink of one of you, let him submerge it (entirely), then take it out, for in one of its wings is a disease and in the other is a cure."
"812","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas that the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) entered the house of Aishah and saw some meat. He said: Roast some of it for us. They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is charity. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Roast some of it for us, for it has reached its destination."
"813","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah who said: I knew that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) was fasting, so I prepared to break his fast with a nabidh I had made in a gourd. Then I brought it to him, and it was bubbling. He said: ""Strike this against the wall, for this is the drink of one who does not believe in Allah and the Last Day."
"814","[AI-translation] Hasan bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), raised to the Prophet: ""Feed the food and sweeten the speech."
"815","[AI-translation] From Muhammad bin Ziyad who said: Abdullah bin Al-Harith used to pass by us and say: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Feed the food and spread the salam, you will inherit the paradises."
"816","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) gave me some dates, so I put them in our basket and hung it on the ceiling of the house. We continued eating from it until the end of it, which was seized by the people of Sham when they raided Al-Madinah."
"817","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin Samurah: A man had a she-camel in Al-Harrah, and he handed it over to a man while it had become ill. When it was about to die, his wife said to him, ""If only you slaughtered it and we ate from it."" He refused and went to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) and mentioned that to him. He asked, ""Do you have anything to suffice you?"" He replied, ""No."" He said, ""Then eat it"" – meaning the she-camel – and it had died. He said: We ate from its grease, its meat, and its fat for about twenty days. Then its owner met him and said to him, ""Would that you had slaughtered it?"" He replied, ""I was too shy before you."
"818","[AI-translation] From Jabir: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) passed by a donkey that had been branded on its face. He said: ""Has it not reached you that I have cursed the one who brands the beast in its face, or strikes it in its face?!"" And he forbade that."
"819","[AI-translation] From Salim bin Abdullah bin Umar, from his father: That the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) commanded to sharpen the blades and to conceal them from the animals. When one of you slaughters, let him do it swiftly."
"820","On the authority of Umm ʿAbdullāh, the sister of Shaddād ibn Aws, who said: She sent to the Prophet ﷺ a cup of milk at the time of his breaking fast, and that was during a long day and intense heat. He sent back his messenger to her, saying: ""How did you come by this milk?"" She said: ""Milk from a sheep of mine."" He sent back his messenger to her: ""How did you come by this sheep?"" She said: ""I bought it with my own money."" So he drank it. When the next day came, Umm ʿAbdullāh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I sent you that milk out of compassion for you, because of the length of the day and the severity of the heat, yet you sent back your messenger concerning it?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""The messengers before me were commanded not to eat except what is pure (ṭayyib), and not to act except righteously."""
"821","[AI-translation] From Sa'id bin Khalid who said: I entered upon Abu Salamah, and he brought us butter and a lump. A fly fell into the food, so Abu Salamah began to dip it with his finger into it. I said: ""O uncle! What are you doing?"" He said: ""Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) who said: 'Indeed, one of the wings of a fly is poison and the other is a cure. So if it falls into the food, dip it, for it presents the poison and delays the cure.'"
"822","[AI-translation] From Ibrahim bin Sa'd, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I heard Ammar bin Yasir at Siffin on the day he was killed, and he was calling out: ""Paradise has been brought near, and the wide-eyed houris have been wed. Today we meet our beloved Muhammad (peace be upon him and his family)."" And in a narration: ""Today we meet the beloved ones, Muhammad and his party. He made a covenant to me that the last of your provision from the world will be a sip of milk."
"823","[AI-translation] From Umm Salamah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the one who drinks from a vessel of silver (or gold) is only gargling the fire of Hell in his belly, unless he repents."
"824","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Indeed, Allah is pleased with the servant when he eats a meal and praises Him for it, or drinks a drink and praises Him for it."
"825","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, raised to the Prophet: ""The blessing is in the middle of the platter, so eat from its sides and do not eat from its top."
"826","Aisha said: Umm Sunbula brought milk as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). She came to me with it but did not find him. I said to her: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) has forbidden us from eating the food of the Bedouins."" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) and Abu Bakr entered. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""O Umm Sunbula! What is this with you?"" She said: ""Milk, O Messenger of Allah, I brought it as a gift for you."" He said: ""Pour it, O Umm Sunbula, and give it to Abu Bakr."" Then he said: ""Pour it, O Umm Sunbula, and give it to Aisha."" Then he said: ""Pour it, O Umm Sunbula."" So she gave it to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and he drank. She said: I said: ""How cool it is on the liver, O Messenger of Allah! You had forbidden the food of the Bedouins."" He said: ""O Aisha! They are not Bedouins; they are the people of our desert, and we are the people of their settlement. And when they are called, they respond. So they are not Bedouins."""
"827","[AI-translation] From 'Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, forbade visiting the graves, and from the vessels, and that the meat of sacrificial animals be kept after three [days]. Then he said: ""I had forbidden you from visiting the graves, so visit them, for they remind you of the Hereafter. And I forbade you from the vessels, so drink from them, and avoid every intoxicant. And I forbade you from the meat of the sacrificial animals being kept after three [days], so keep it as long as you wish."
"828","[AI-translation] Khattab, raised to the Prophet: ""The food of one suffices for two, and the food of two suffices for three and four, and the food of four suffices for five and six."
"829","[AI-translation] Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Indeed, there is wine from grapes, and indeed there is wine from dates, and indeed there is wine from honey, and indeed there is wine from wheat, and indeed there is wine from barley."
"830","[AI-translation] From a man among the Companions of the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Indeed, some people of my Ummah will drink wine, calling it by other than its name."
"831","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah ibn 'Ukaym, he said: Our shaykhs from Juhaynah said that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, wrote to them: ""Do not derive any benefit from the carrion."
"832","[AI-translation] Hudhali, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""We used to forbid you from eating its meat beyond three [days] so that it would suffice you, but Allah has brought abundance, so eat, store, and trade. Verily, these days are days of eating, drinking, and remembering Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"833","[AI-translation] From Fayruz, he said: We came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, you know who we are and where we come from. To whom do we belong?"" He said: ""To Allah and to His Messenger."" We said: ""O Messenger of Allah, we have grapes, what should we do with them?"" He said: ""Make them into raisins."" We said: ""What should we do with the raisins?"" He said: ""Steep them for your morning meal and drink them for your evening meal, and steep them for your evening meal and drink them for your morning meal. And steep them in skins, and do not steep them in earthenware jars, for if it is delayed past its pressing, it becomes vinegar."
"834","[AI-translation] From Asma' bint Abi Bakr: That when she made tharid, she would cover it with something until its heat and smoke went away, then she would say: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: 'Indeed, it is greater for blessing.'"
"835","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""It is blessed; it is food that nourishes.""Abu Dharr reported: We departed from our people, Ghifar, and they used to consider the sacred month permissible. So I set out with my brother Unays and our mother, and we alighted with an uncle of ours. Our uncle honored us and treated us well, but his people envied us. They said: ""When you left your family, Unays turned against them."" So our uncle came to us and conveyed to us what had been said to him. I said: ""As for the kindness you showed us previously, you have spoiled it, and you have no claim over us after this."" So we prepared our provisions, loaded them onto our camels, and our uncle covered himself with his garment and wept. We departed until we alighted near Mecca.Unays gambled away our provisions and their like. They went to a soothsayer who ruled in favor of Unays, and Unays returned to us with our provisions and their like with them.He said: ""I had prayed, O son of my brother, for three years before I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" I said: ""For whom?"" He said: ""For Allah."" I said: ""Which direction did you face?"" He said: ""I face wherever my Lord directs me. I pray the evening prayer until the last part of the night, then I fall down as if I were a cloak until the sun rises over me.""Unays said: ""I have a need in Mecca, so suffice me."" Unays went until he came to Mecca, then returned to me. I said: ""What did you do?"" He said: ""I met a man in Mecca upon your religion who claims that Allah has sent him."" I said: ""What do the people say?"" He said: ""They say: A poet, a soothsayer, a sorcerer."" And Unays was one of the poets. Unays said: ""I have heard the speech of soothsayers, and this is not like their speech. I have compared his words to the meters of poetry, and it does not conform to the tongue of any poet after me. By Allah, he is truthful, and they are liars.""I said: ""Suffice me until I go and see."" So I came to Mecca and feigned weakness before a man from them. I said: ""Where is this man whom you call the Sabi?"" He pointed to me and said: ""The Sabi!"" So the people of the valley pelted me with every stone and bone until I fell unconscious. I rose when I rose as if I were a red idol. I came to Zamzam, washed the blood from myself, and drank from its water. I remained, O son of my brother, thirty days and nights with no food except Zamzam water. I grew fat until the folds of my belly cracked, and I found no pangs of hunger in my liver.While the people of Mecca were in a moonlit, bright night, sleep overtook them. No one circumambulated the House except two women from them invoking Isaf and Na'ilah. They passed by me in their circumambulation. I said: ""Marry one of them to the other."" They did not desist from their invocation. They passed by me again and I said: ""They are like a piece of wood, except that I do not use a euphemism."" They departed wailing and saying: ""Would that there were someone from our clansmen here!""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr met them, descending. He said: ""What is the matter with you two?"" They said: ""The Sabi is between the Ka'bah and its coverings."" He said: ""What did he say to you?"" They said: ""He said a word to us that fills the mouth.""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came until he touched the Stone and circumambulated the House, he and his companion. Then he prayed. When he finished his prayer, Abu Dharr said: I was the first to greet him with the greeting of Islam. I said: ""Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""And upon you be the mercy of Allah."" Then he said: ""Who are you?"" I said: ""From Ghifar."" He gestured with his hand and placed his finger on his forehead. I said to myself: ""He dislikes that I belong to Ghifar."" I went to take his hand, but his companion restrained me—he knew him better than I. Then he raised his head and said: ""How long have you been here?"" I said: ""I have been here for thirty days and nights."" He said: ""Who has been feeding you?"" I said: ""I have had no food except Zamzam water. I grew fat until the folds of my belly cracked, and I find no pangs of hunger in my liver."" He said: ""It is blessed; it is food that nourishes.""Abu Bakr said: ""O Messenger of Allah, permit me to feed him tonight."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr went, and I went with them. Abu Bakr opened a door and began handing us raisins from Ta'if. That was the first food I ate there.Then I stayed for a while, then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: ""A land of palm trees has been shown to me, and I see it only as Yathrib. Will you convey my message to your people? Perhaps Allah will benefit them through you and reward you among them.""I came to Unays and he said: ""What did you do?"" I said: ""I have submitted and believed."" He said: ""I have no aversion to your religion, for I have submitted and believed."" We came to our mother and she said: ""I have no aversion to your religion, for I have submitted and believed.""We departed until we came to our people, Ghifar. Half of them embraced Islam, led by Aymah ibn Rahadah al-Ghifari, their chief. The other half said: ""When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrives in Medina, we will embrace Islam."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Medina, and the remaining half embraced Islam.Aslam came and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, they are our brothers; we embrace Islam upon what they embraced Islam upon."" So they embraced Islam.The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Ghifar—Allah has forgiven her; Aslam—Allah has granted her safety."""
"836","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, was brought milk mixed with water. On his right was a bedouin, and on his left was Abu Bakr. He drank, then gave it to the bedouin and said: ""The right, then the right."" And in another narration: ""The right ones, the right ones. So give to the right."
"837","[AI-translation] It was narrated from a man who served the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, for eight years, that he used to hear the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, when food was brought to him, say: ""In the name of Allah."" And when he finished, he would say: ""O Allah, You have fed, given drink, made independent, guided, and given life, so to You is praise for what You have given."
"838","[AI-translation] It was narrated from 'Aishah that they slaughtered a sheep, and the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""What remains of it?"" She said: ""Nothing remains of it except its shoulder."" He said: ""All of it remains except its shoulder."
"839","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Salma that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""A house in which there are no dates is like a house in which there is no food."
"840","[AI-translation] 'Abdullah bin 'Umar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Three will Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, not look at on the Day of Resurrection: the one undutiful to his parents, the woman who imitates men, and the dayyouth. And three will not enter Paradise: the one undutiful to his parents, the chronic drinker of khamr, and the one who boasts of what he gives."
"841","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Salim bin 'Abdullah (bin 'Umar) from his father from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""Allah has forbidden khamr, and every intoxicant is haram."
"842","[AI-translation] ( ) He said, peace be upon him: ""The best of your dates is al-barni; it takes away disease and there is no disease in it."" Narrated from the hadith of Buraidah bin Al-Husayb, and Anas bin Malik, and Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri, and narrated ???? bin 'Abdullah, 'Ali bin Abi Talib, and some ???? of 'Abd Al-Qais."
"843","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""Khamr is from these two trees: the date palm and the grapevine."" ( )"
"844","[AI-translation] Azwar that he said: My family sent me with a milch camel - and in a narration: a milch she-camel - to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family. So I brought it to him, and he ordered me to milk it, then he said: ""Leave the froth of the milk."
"845","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Abu Hurairah, elevated to the Prophet: ""The blood of an 'Afra' is more beloved to Allah than the blood of two black ones."
"846","[AI-translation] Qurashi who said: We entered the house of Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family), and found in it 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas. We mentioned the ablution [required] from what the fire has touched. 'Abdullah said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) eating what the fire had touched, then praying without performing ablution. One of us said to him: Did you see him, O Ibn 'Abbas? He said: So he pointed with his hand to his eyes and said: With the sight of my eyes."
"847","On the authority of Thābit, from Anas ibn Mālik, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Umm Ḥarām. We brought him dates and clarified butter. He said: ""Return this to its vessel and this to its waterskin, for I am fasting."" Then he stood and led us in two rakʿahs of voluntary prayer. Umm Ḥarām and Umm Sulaym stood behind us, and he positioned me on his right side, as Thābit reckons. He led us in voluntary prayer upon a mat. When he finished his prayer, Umm Sulaym said: ""I have a special request: your servant Anas—supplicate to Allah for him."" He did not leave any good of this world or the Hereafter that day except that he supplicated for me with it. Then he said: ""O Allah, increase his wealth and his children, and bless him therein."" Anas said: ""My daughter informed me that I have been granted from my own loins ninety-odd (descendants), and no man among the Anṣār woke up possessing more wealth than I."" Then Anas said: ""O Thābit! I do not own any gold or silver except my ring."""
"848","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) was brought some Rayyan dates. He said: Where did you get this? They said: We had Ba'al dates, so we sold two sa's for one sa. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return it to its owner (meaning: the Rayyan), and sell it (meaning: the inferior dates) for cash, then buy the dates."
"849","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, raised [to the Prophet]: The worst of food is the food of the wedding feast; it is withheld from those who come to it, and those who refuse it are invited to it. Whoever does not answer the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"850","[AI-translation] From Anas, raised [to the Prophet]: He said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) performed the 'Aqiqah for himself after he was sent as a Prophet."
"851","[AI-translation] From Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, raised [to the Prophet]: Cover the vessel and tie the waterskin, for indeed in the year there is a night in which a pestilence descends. It does not pass by any vessel that has no cover over it, or any waterskin that has no tying over it, except that some of that pestilence descends into it."
"852","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A tribe from the Children of Israel was lost; it is not known what they did. And I do not see them except as the rats. Do you not see that when camel milk is placed for them they do not drink it, and when sheep milk is placed for them they drink it?"
"853","ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I brought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) a khazīrah I had cooked for him. I said to Sawdah, while the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was between me and her: ""Eat."" She refused. I said: ""By Allah, you will eat, or I will smear your face."" She refused, so I put my hand in the khazīrah and smeared her face with it. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) laughed, then placed his thigh for her and said to Sawdah: ""Smear her face."" So she smeared my face. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) laughed again. Then ʿUmar passed by and called out: ""O ʿAbdullāh! O ʿAbdullāh!"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) thought he would enter, so he said to them both: ""Get up and wash your faces""—meaning ʿĀʾishah and Sawdah. ʿĀʾishah said: ""I continued to stand in awe of ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) because of the Messenger of Allah's (peace and blessings be upon him) awe of him."""
"854","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah who said: The most beloved of drinks to him was the sweet and cold."
"855","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah who said: The most beloved of meaty bones to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) was the foreleg of the sheep."
"856","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah who said: When he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) ate food, he would eat from what was in front of him."
"857","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik who said: When he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) drank, he would breathe three times and say: It is more wholesome, more nourishing, and more healing."
"858","[AI-translation] Ansari: Whenever the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, ate or drank, he would say: ""Praise is to Allah Who fed, gave drink, made it easy to swallow, and made for it an exit."
"859","[AI-translation] Khudri: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, had forbidden us from eating the meat of our sacrificial animals beyond three days. He said: I went out on a journey and then returned to my family some days after al-Adha. My wife came to me with a cooked dish in which she had put dried meat. I said to her: ""Where did you get this dried meat?"" She said: ""From our sacrificial animals."" I said to her: ""Did the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, not forbid us from eating them beyond three days?"" She said: ""Indeed, permission was granted to the people after that."" He said: I did not believe her until I sent to my brother Qatadah ibn al-Nu'man, who was present at Badr, to ask him about that. He sent to me saying: ""Eat your food, for she has spoken the truth; the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, granted permission to the Muslims regarding that."
"860","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah ibn Busr: The Prophet, peace be upon him, had a bowl called al-Gharra' which four men could carry."
"861","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, used to eat watermelon with fresh dates, and he would say: ""We break the heat of this with the coldness of this, and the coldness of this with the heat of this."
"862","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: The Prophet, peace be upon him, used to eat fresh dates with melon, meaning watermelon."
"863","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah ibn Ja'far: The Prophet, peace be upon him, used to eat cucumber with fresh dates."
"864","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas ibn Malik: Dates containing worms would be brought to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he would inspect them, extracting the worms from them."
"865","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas ibn Malik: The Prophet, peace be upon him, loved gourd."
"866","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: The Prophet, peace be upon him, used to drink in three breaths. When he brought the vessel close to his mouth, he would mention the name of Allah the Exalted, and when he moved it away, he would praise Allah. He would do that three times."
"867","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah: The Prophet, peace be upon him, liked sweet, cold things."
"868","[AI-translation] From Jabir, he said: Nabidh would be prepared for the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) in a waterskin, and if there was no waterskin, then in a stoneware jar."
"869","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Every beast of prey with fangs, eating it is unlawful."
"870","[AI-translation] Bahili (may Allah be pleased with him), raised to the Prophet (peace be upon him): ""Eat that which severs the jugular veins, as long as it is not the tearing of a fang or the piercing of a claw."
"871","[AI-translation] He (peace be upon him) said: ""Eat what your bow returns to you."" It is narrated from the hadith of Abdullah bin Umar, Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, Uqbah bin Amir, and Hudhayfah bin al-Yaman."
"872","[AI-translation] Asqa' al-Laithi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) took the top of the tharid and said: ""Eat in the name of Allah from its sides, and leave its top, for the blessing comes to it from above."
"873","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Busr, he said: A sheep was gifted to the Prophet ﷺ, and food was scarce that day. So he said to his family: ""Cook this sheep, and look at this flour, bake it and cook it, and make tharid with it."" He said: And the Prophet ﷺ had a large bowl called al-Gharra', which four men would carry. When morning came and they prayed the Duha prayer, that bowl was brought and they gathered around it. When the people became numerous, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat on his knees. A Bedouin said: ""What is this sitting posture?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Allah made me a generous servant and did not make me a tyrannical, stubborn one."" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Eat from its sides, and leave its top, it will be blessed for you in it."" Then he said: ""Take and eat, for by the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, Allah will surely open up to you the lands of Persia and Rome, until food becomes abundant so that the name of Allah is not mentioned."""
"874","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Eat olive oil and anoint yourselves with it, for it is from a blessed tree."
"875","[AI-translation] From Ubaidullah bin Abu Yazid, his father informed him, saying: I lodged with Umm Ayyub, with whom the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) had lodged. I stayed with her and she narrated to me this from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), that they prepared some food containing certain herbs and presented it, but he disliked it and said to his companions: ""Eat (meaning: the garlic), for I am not like anyone of you, for I fear that I may offend my companion (meaning: the angel)."
"876","[AI-translation] From Aishah, she said: Ali arrived to us from a journey, and we presented to him from it (the sacrificial meat), so he said: ""I will not eat it until I ask the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) about it."" She said: So Ali asked him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Eat it from Dhu al-Hijjah to Dhu al-Hijjah,"" meaning the meat of the sacrificial animals."
"877","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, he said: ""We used to call it Shabba'ah, meaning Zamzam, and we found it to be an excellent help for the family."
"878","[AI-translation] From Sulaiman bin Buraidah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""I used to forbid you from keeping the meat of the sacrificial animals for more than three days, so that those with means might extend to those without means. So eat as you wish, feed others, and store it."
"879","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah he said: When this verse was revealed: ""There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have tasted, if they are conscious of God and believe and do righteous deeds, then are conscious of God and believe, then are conscious of God and do good. And God loves the good-doers"" [93], he said to me: It was said to me: You are among them."
"880","[AI-translation] 'Aliya bint Subay' she said: I had sheep at Uhud and death befell them. I entered upon Maimuna, the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, and mentioned that to her. She said: If only you had taken their skins and benefited from them. I said: Is that permissible? She said: Yes. Men from Quraysh passed by the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, dragging a sheep of theirs like a donkey. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to them: If only you had taken its hide. They said: It is carrion. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, said: Water and acacia bark purify it."
"881","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayra he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If the one who drinks while standing knew what is in his stomach, he would vomit it."
"882","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayra: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, said: Let one of you eat with his right hand, drink with his right hand, take with his right hand, and give with his right hand. For Satan eats with his left, drinks with his left, gives with his left, and takes with his left."
"883","[AI-translation] From Umm Hani' she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, entered upon me and said: O Umm Hani', do you have anything? She said: No, except dry pieces of bread and vinegar. He said: How destitute is a house of Adam that has vinegar."
"884","[AI-translation] Kindi he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, say: No human fills a vessel worse than his stomach. It is sufficient for the son of Adam to eat a few mouthfuls to keep his back straight. But if he must, then a third for his food, a third for his drink, and a third for his breath."
"885","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The wine addict, if he dies, meets God as an idol worshipper."
"886","[AI-translation] From Jundub ibn 'Abd Allah he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever among you is able not to let a handful of a Muslim's blood that he spills intervene between him and Paradise, as if he were slaughtering a chicken with it; every time he approaches a gate of the gates of Paradise, God intervenes between him and it. And whoever is able not to place anything in his stomach except what is good, for the first thing of a person to rot is his stomach."
"887","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, raised to the Prophet: Whoever eats dates with a people and wants to eat them in pairs, let him seek their permission."
"888","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I entered upon my aunt Maymunah, and Khalid ibn al-Walid was with her. Maymunah said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Will you not eat from what my brother gifted me from the desert?"" So she brought two roasted lizards on a platter. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Eat, for it is not from the food of my people; I find myself averse to it."" And Ibn Abbas and Khalid ate from it. Maymunah said: ""I will not eat from food that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not eat from."" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked for a drink, and a vessel of milk was brought. He drank, and on his right was Ibn Abbas and on his left was Khalid ibn al-Walid. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ibn Abbas: ""Will you permit me to give Khalid to drink?"" Ibn Abbas said: ""I would not love to give anyone preference over myself with the leftover of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" So Ibn Abbas took it and drank, and Khalid drank. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Whoever Allah feeds with food, let him say: O Allah, bless us in it and provide us with better than it. And whoever Allah gives milk to drink, let him say: O Allah, bless us in it and increase us from it, for I do not know of anything that suffices as both food and drink except milk."""
"889","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, raised to the Prophet: Whoever spends the night while there is grease on his hand, and something afflicts him, let him blame none but himself."
"890","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Huraira from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) that he said on the Day of Sacrifice: Whoever slaughtered - I think he said - before the prayer, let him repeat his slaughter."
"891","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: Whoever forgets to mention Allah at the beginning of his food, let him say when he remembers: ""In the name of Allah at its beginning and its end."" For indeed it entails beginning a new meal, and it prevents the evil one from taking whatever he was taking from it."
"892","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Huraira, marfu'an: The two competitors are not to be answered, nor is their food to be eaten."
"893","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas: He (peace be upon him and his family) forbade us to drink from the broken vessel."
"894","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Huraira: The Prophet (peace be upon him) forbade drinking from the mouth of the waterskin. Ayyub said: I was informed that a man drank from the mouth of the waterskin, and a snake came out."
"895","[AI-translation] Narrated Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her: He (peace be upon him and his family) forbade drinking from the mouth of the waterskin because that spoils it."
"896","[AI-translation] Aliya: Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri was asked (and in a narration: I asked Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri) about the nabidh of jars. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) forbade the nabidh of jars."
"897","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Huraira: He forbade drinking from the broken edge of the bowl."
"898","[AI-translation] Khudri: The Prophet (peace be upon him) forbade the bending of the waterskins."
"899","[AI-translation] Rahman ibn Shabl: He (peace be upon him and his family) forbade eating the dabb lizard."
"900","[AI-translation] Darda': He (peace be upon him) forbade eating the *mujaththamah*, which is the animal targeted with arrows."
"901","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik: He (peace be upon him and his family) forbade eating and drinking from gold and silver vessels."
"902","[AI-translation] From Abu Sa'id: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) forbade garlic, onions, and leeks."
"903","[AI-translation] From Anas: He (peace be upon him) — in one wording: reprimanded — forbade drinking while standing."
"904","[AI-translation] Khudri: He (peace be upon him) forbade drinking from the broken edge of a cup and blowing into the drink."
"905","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar who said: He (peace be upon him and his family) forbade two types of eating: sitting at a table upon which alcohol is drunk, and a man eating while lying prone on his stomach."
"906","[AI-translation] Khudri: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) forbade blowing into the drink. A man said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I am not quenched with a single breath."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to him: ""Then remove the cup from your mouth and breathe."" He said: ""What if I see a speck in it?"" He said: ""Then pour it out."
"907","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin Abdullah who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) forbade the meat of domesticated donkeys on the day of Khaybar, and permitted the meat of horses."
"908","[AI-translation] and it is said: Ibn Abi Tariq — who said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) in his house, and he had these *dubba'* (gourds). I said: ""What is this?"" He said: ""This is the *qar'*, it is the *dubba'*; we increase our food with it."
"909","[AI-translation] Khushani who said: I came to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, tell me what is lawful for me from what is forbidden upon me."" He said: ""Do not eat the domesticated donkey, nor any predator with fangs."
"910","[AI-translation] From Abu Musa who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, sent me to Yemen. I said: O Messenger of Allah, there are drinks there, so what should I drink and what should I leave? He said: And what are they? I said: Bit' and Mizr. He said: And what are Bit' and Mizr? I said: As for Bit', it is the nabidh of honey, and as for Mizr, it is the nabidh of millet. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, then said: Do not drink any intoxicant, for I have forbidden every intoxicant."
"911","On the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās, that the delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays said: ""O Messenger of Allah, in what vessels may we drink?"" He said: ""Do not drink from the ḍubbāʾ (gourd vessels), nor from the muzaffat (pitch-coated vessels), nor from the naqīr (hollowed-out tree trunks), and steep (your drinks) in the asqiya (water skins)."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah, what if it becomes strong (ferments) in the asqiya?"" He said: ""Then pour water over it."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah…"" So he said to them on the third or fourth time: ""Pour it out."" Then he said: ""Indeed Allah has forbidden to me — or wine has been forbidden — and the maysir (gambling) and the kūba."" He said: ""And every intoxicant is ḥarām."" Sufyān said: So I asked ʿAlī ibn Bādhima about the kūba, and he said: ""The drum (ṭabl)."""
"912","[AI-translation] From Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: There is no 'Aqr in Islam."
"913","[AI-translation] From Ata who said: A woman said in the presence of Aishah: If so-and-so's wife had given birth, we would have slaughtered a camel on his behalf. Aishah said: No, but the Sunnah for a boy is two sheep and for a girl is one sheep."
"914","[AI-translation] Darda from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: No one undutiful to parents, nor an addict of wine, nor a denier of Qadar will enter Paradise."
"915","[AI-translation] From Abdullah ibn Amr from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: No one undutiful to parents, nor one who reminds others of his favors, nor an addict of wine, (nor a child of Zina) will enter Paradise."
"916","[AI-translation] Ash'ari who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: An addict of wine will not enter Paradise, nor one who believes in Sihr, nor one who severs ties of kinship."
"917","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: None of you should drink while standing."
"918","[AI-translation] From Umar ibn Abi Salamah who said: I was a boy in the care of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and my hand used to roam around the plate, so the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said to me: O boy, when you eat, say Bismillah, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is in front of you."
